@page
@model IndexModel

<section>
    <h2>1. HtmxUrlTagHelper — <code>hx-page</code> + <code>hx-page-handler</code></h2>
    <p>Uses <code>hx-page</code> and <code>hx-page-handler</code> attributes to generate HTMX URLs:</p>
    <button hx-page="/Index"
            hx-page-handler="ServerTime"
            hx-target="#result">Get Server Time</button>
    <button hx-page="/Index"
            hx-page-handler="Hello"
            hx-target="#result">Say Hello</button>
    <div id="result" class="result"></div>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>2. HtmxUrlTagHelper — route parameters via <code>hx-route-*</code> and <code>hx-all-route-data</code></h2>
    <button hx-get
            hx-page="/Index"
            hx-page-handler="Greet"
            hx-route-name="World"
            hx-target="#greet-result">Greet via <b>hx-route-*</b></button>
    <button hx-get
            hx-page="/Index"
            hx-page-handler="Greet"
            hx-all-route-data="@(new Dictionary<string, string> { { "name", "HTMX" } })"
            hx-target="#greet-result">Greet via <b>hx-all-route-data</b></button>
    <div id="greet-result" class="result"></div>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>3. HtmxHeaderTagHelper — <code>hx-header-*</code> attributes</h2>
    <p>Custom headers added via <code>hx-header-*</code> attributes. The server reads them and triggers client-side events:</p>
    <button hx-get
            hx-page="/Index"
            hx-page-handler="CustomHeader"
            hx-header-Custom-Header="MyValue"
            hx-target="#header-result">Send with Custom Header</button>
    <div id="header-result" class="result"></div>

    <script>
        document.addEventListener("customEvent", e => console.log("customEvent:", e.detail.message));
        document.addEventListener("logEvent", e => console.log("logEvent:", e.detail.message));
    </script>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>4. Fluent API — <code>Response.Htmx()</code></h2>
    <p>Setting HTMX response headers via the fluent API in the page handler:</p>
    <div style="display:flex; gap:8px; flex-wrap:wrap;">
        <button hx-get
                hx-page="/Index"
                hx-page-handler="Reswap"
                hx-target="#fluent-result"
                hx-swap="outerHTML">
            Reswap (AfterBegin)
        </button>
        <button hx-get
                hx-page="/Index"
                hx-page-handler="Retarget"
                hx-target="#this-should-be-ignored">
            Retarget to #result
        </button>
        <span id="this-should-be-ignored" style="display:none;"></span>
    </div>
    <div id="fluent-result" class="result"></div>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>5. Polling with <code>StopPolling()</code></h2>
    <p hx-get
       hx-page="/Index"
       hx-page-handler="StopPolling"
       hx-target="#poll-result"
       hx-trigger="every 1s"
       hx-swap="innerHTML">The server randomly stops polling via <code>h.StopPolling(condition)</code>:</p>
    <div id="poll-result" class="result"></div>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>6. <code>IsHtmxRequest()</code> — detect HTMX vs full page requests</h2>
    <p>Use <code>Request.IsHtmxRequest()</code> in handlers to return different content:</p>
    <button hx-get
            hx-page="/Index"
            hx-page-handler="PartialOrFull"
            hx-target="#partial-result">Fetch via HTMX</button>
    <a asp-page="/Index" asp-page-handler="PartialOrFull" target="_blank">Open as full page request</a>
    <div id="partial-result" class="result"></div>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>7. <code>Response.Htmx()</code> — imperative response headers</h2>
    <p>Setting <code>h.Reswap(HtmxSwap.InnerHtml)</code> programmatically in the handler:</p>
    <button hx-get
            hx-page="/Index"
            hx-page-handler="DeclarativeReswap"
            hx-target="#declarative-result"
            hx-swap="outerHTML">Fetch (swaps with InnerHtml)</button>
    <div id="declarative-result" class="result"></div>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>8. <code>IsHtmxBoosted()</code> — detect boosted links</h2>
    <p>Use <code>hx-boost=&quot;true&quot;</code> on a link to make it an AJAX request:</p>
    <a asp-page="/Index" asp-page-handler="BoostedCheck" hx-boost="true" hx-target="#boosted-result">Click this boosted link</a>
    <div id="boosted-result" class="result"></div>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>9. Random number (click to load)</h2>
    <button hx-get
            hx-page="/Index"
            hx-page-handler="Random"
            hx-target="#random-result">Get Random Number</button>
    <div id="random-result" class="result"></div>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>10. Antiforgery Token — form submission via <code>hx-post</code></h2>
    <p>The antiforgery token is automatically included in every HTMX request by
       <code>&lt;meta htmx-config include-antiforgery-token="true" /&gt;</code>
       and the auto-loaded <code>htmx-toolkit.js</code> script
       (<code>@@Html.HtmxAntiforgeryScriptPath()</code>).
       No manual token handling required in the form.</p>
    <form hx-post
          hx-page="/Index"
          hx-page-handler="FormSubmit"
          hx-target="#form-result">
        <p><label><b>Name:</b><br/><input type="text" name="name" placeholder="John Doe" /></label></p>
        <p><label><b>Email:</b><br/><input type="email" name="email" placeholder="john@example.com" /></label></p>
        <p><label><b>Message:</b><br/><textarea name="message" rows="3" placeholder="Your message..."></textarea></label></p>
        <button type="submit">Submit via HTMX</button>
    </form>
    <div id="form-result" class="result"></div>
</section>
